course: dictionary
lesson: 13105
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. To find the right one, read the words around it and ask which meaning fits. «The horse rested its tired flank against the fence.» The fence is next to the horse's side, so flank means the side of its body, between the ribs and the hip.
explain: Flank can also mean the side of a group or a place. «The soldiers attacked the enemy on the left flank.» The clues are soldiers and attacked: an army has sides, and the flank is its weak side, so this means the side of the army.
explain: Flank can also be a verb, an action word. «The president was flanked by two guards.» The guards stand beside him, so flanked means was at the side of. Check by swapping in the meaning: «The president was at the side of two guards» still makes sense, so you have found the right meaning.
fact: Flank means the side of something.
fact: As a noun, a flank can be the side of an animal's or person's body, or the side of an army, a team formation or a building.
fact: As a verb, «flanked» means to be at the side of someone or something.
fact: The phrase «flanked by» means one thing is standing on each side of another, as in «flanked by guards».
fact: In sport, a player on the flank, or wing, runs down the side of the pitch.
exercise: «The horse twitched the skin on its flank to shake off a fly.» What is the flank here? | * The side of the horse's body | The horse's head | The end of the field | A kind of saddle
exercise: «The players ran down the flank to pass the ball.» Where did the players run? | Round the top of the goal | Under the bench | Into the changing room | * Along the side of the pitch
exercise: «The singer was flanked by two dancers on stage.» What does flanked mean? | Ran away from | * Stood at the side of | Fell down beside | Sang loudly over
test: «The army attacked the enemy's flank while the main force held the bridge.» What is the flank in this sentence? | * The weak side of the enemy's army | The front door of the enemy's camp | The river below the bridge | The top of the bridge
test: «The castle was guarded on its north flank by a tall wall.» Which part of the castle is the flank? | The cellar | The main gate | The roof | * The side
exam: «The prince, flanked by knights, rode into the village.» What does flanked mean here? | Was lost from | Was followed by | Was chased by | * Rode at the side of
